meta {
  name: Get People
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/people?email={{testUserEmail}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  email: {{testUserEmail}}
  ~locationId:
  ~max:
  ~id:
  ~displayName:
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Use this to get all of the details of a given person. Useful for pulling back license ID's etc to
  build further downstream requests that need that detail — the List People endpoint.

  **Parameters**
  - `email` (query, active) — filters to the person with this exact email address. Bound to the
    collection variable `{{testUserEmail}}`.
  - `locationId`, `max`, `displayName`, `id` (query, disabled) — alternative filters you can enable
    instead of (or alongside) `email`: scope to a Location, cap the page size, match a display name,
    or look up a specific Person ID.

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/people/list-people

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
